{#- modules/guardrails/ai-coding-maturity.j2
    Shared framing and the established Coding Agents Maturity Model.

    These slides intentionally use the current vis-* compatibility layer so they
    match the modern SANS/Zenable decks while the primitive migration described
    in AGENTS.md is still underway. -#}

{%- macro why_guardrails() -%}
<section class="vis-slide" data-label="Why guardrails">
  <div class="vis-label">The operating reality</div>
  <div class="vis-title">Faster delivery changes the risk equation</div>
  <div class="vis-subtitle">Generative AI is becoming a default part of the software development lifecycle.</div>

  <div class="vis-grid-2" style="flex:1; gap:30px; align-items:stretch; padding:26px 0;">
    <div class="vis-teal-card" style="padding:28px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; justify-content:center;">
      <p style="font-size:12px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.18em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#2dd4bf; margin:0 0 18px 0;">What accelerates</p>
      <p style="font-size:46px; font-weight:800; color:#fff; line-height:1.08; margin:0 0 18px 0;">Code volume<br>and change velocity</p>
      <p style="font-size:16px; color:#94a3b8; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">More experiments, more pull requests, and more decisions made before a human sees the diff.</p>
    </div>

    <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:12px;">
      <div class="vis-red-card" style="padding:20px;">
        <p style="font-size:28px; margin:0 0 10px 0;">🔓</p>
        <p style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; color:#fff; margin:0 0 7px 0;">Security risk</p>
        <p style="font-size:13px; color:#94a3b8; margin:0; line-height:1.5;">Unsafe defaults and insecure patterns propagate quickly.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vis-amber-card" style="padding:20px;">
        <p style="font-size:28px; margin:0 0 10px 0;">🧱</p>
        <p style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; color:#fff; margin:0 0 7px 0;">Operational fragility</p>
        <p style="font-size:13px; color:#94a3b8; margin:0; line-height:1.5;">Locally plausible code can violate system-wide assumptions.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vis-purple-card" style="padding:20px;">
        <p style="font-size:28px; margin:0 0 10px 0;">🔎</p>
        <p style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; color:#fff; margin:0 0 7px 0;">Review overload</p>
        <p style="font-size:13px; color:#94a3b8; margin:0; line-height:1.5;">Human review capacity does not scale with generated code.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="vis-blue-card" style="padding:20px;">
        <p style="font-size:28px; margin:0 0 10px 0;">📋</p>
        <p style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; color:#fff; margin:0 0 7px 0;">Audit gaps</p>
        <p style="font-size:13px; color:#94a3b8; margin:0; line-height:1.5;">Intent and decision evidence disappear after the fact.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="vis-callout vis-callout-teal" style="text-align:center;">
    The answer is not less AI. It is a <strong>control system that scales with AI</strong>.
  </div>
</section>
{%- endmacro -%}


